findings.claim:
Three items of Fontaine's almost de Rham theory and Berger's functors are marked planned at PadicHodgeTheory:P7:
- 3.1-bdr-reps: the category Rep_{B_dR}(G_K) and almost de Rham representations;
- 3.1.1-equivalence: Fontaine's equivalence D_pdR : Rep_pdR(G_K) ≅ Rep_K(G_a);
- 3.3.5-WdR: Berger's W⁺_dR and W_dR on (φ,Γ_K)-modules over R_{A,K}, and their freeness and exactness.
P7 plans none of them. Its stage text is about Robba and annulus coefficient rings, importing étale (φ,Γ)-modules from PG.0–PG.3, and comparing Wach modules with D_cris. Its accepted packet (research/blueprint/packets/PadicHodgeTheory--P7.json) has 60 nodes. They cover Robba rings, the localisation maps ι_n, Sen's D_Sen(V), Fontaine's D_dif(V), D_dR via ι_n and Wach modules. None is the category of B_dR-representations, almost de Rham representations, B_pdR, D_pdR, the G_a-equivalence, or W⁺_dR of a general (φ,Γ_K)-module with coefficients. The extraction is also inconsistent with itself. Route 2's brief says 'Construct almost de Rham B_dR-representations and Fontaine's equivalence W ↦ (D_pdR(W), ν_W) with Rep_K(G_a)', while route 4 sends the same items to P7, and the companion items 3.1-bpdr and 3.1.4-coefficients are missing on route 2. An accepted extraction gives these objects another owner. The PAPER-FARGUES-FONTAINE-18 extraction routes B_dR-representations (its item 941, No 10.4.1) and B-pairs (items 886, 1104) as missing to the PadicHodgeTheory Part II of its route 5. That brief says it will 'export B-pairs and their Tannakian category to The trianguline variety and its local model (TriangulineVarietyAndItsLocalModel), which currently expects them from P7'. B-pairs themselves, and Berger's equivalence between (φ,Γ_K)-modules over R_K and B-pairs, are used in the proof of Proposition 3.5.1 but have no item. Disclosure: this session reviewed PAPER-FARGUES-FONTAINE-18 (PR #4683), including that route 5. PAPER-DING-25 makes the same P7 claim (its items 2.1-bpairs and 2.2-fontaine-bdr).

Item 5.1-patched is marked planned at R31.5 but contains the following:
- R_∞, built from the local deformation rings at all v ∈ S;
- the patched representation Π_∞ of Caraiani–Emerton–Gee–Geraghty–Paškūnas–Shin for GL_n over the p-adic places of a CM field;
- the patched eigenvariety X_p(ρ̄), the support of (J_{B_p}(Π_∞^{R_∞-an}))′;
- its decomposition (5.8) into pieces X^p × ι(X_tri^{X^p-aut}(ρ̄_p)) × U^g.
R31.5 plans 'the patched completed module or the equivalent local–global argument used by the selected lifting theorem' of the GL₂/Q roadmap. It plans neither the CEGGPS module for GL_n, nor a patched eigenvariety, nor Emerton's Jacquet functor, nor anything built on the trianguline variety. The ancestors of R31.5 include no trianguline or Jacquet-functor stage, so (5.8) cannot be proved there. The accepted PAPER-BOCKLE-IYENGAR-PASKUNAS-23 extraction records the CEGGPS patched module M_∞ and its properties (its items 133–134) as missing and routes them to a Part II of the same parent (its route 7). The same object is therefore 'planned at R31.5' in one accepted extraction and 'missing' in another.

The paper uses four inputs from locally analytic representation theory that no item states:
- the Orlik–Strauch functor F^G_{B̄}(M, V);
- the Orlik–Strauch theorem on its irreducibility and Jordan–Hölder constituents, the source of the multiplicities m_{δ,Π} in Conjecture 4.3.4 and Theorem 4.3.8 and of 'each constituent occurs with multiplicity one' in Proposition 4.3.6;
- Emerton's locally analytic Jacquet functor J_B;
- Emerton's adjunction for it.
They appear only inside larger items and in the prerequisites. The accepted PAPER-DING-25 route 1 proposes the new roadmap LocallyAnalyticRepresentationsOfLocalGroups, now queued as DESIGN-LocallyAnalyticRepresentationsOfLocalGroups. Its brief owns exactly these: '(ii) construct the Orlik–Strauch functors F^G_{P^-}(M,π) … and prove the theorem describing their irreducible constituents … (iii) construct Emerton's locally analytic Jacquet functor J_B … and prove the adjunction'. Route 3's brief instead says 'Develop the Orlik–Strauch functor and the adjunction of §5.2 with the exactness criteria on category O', which duplicates that roadmap. The extraction's gap 'orlik-strauch-over-products' is about Remark 5.1.2: the Orlik–Strauch and Emerton results are needed for G_1(K_1) × G_2(K_2) with K_1 ≠ K_2. That obligation belongs with the roadmap that owns those results, and it is not handed to it.

The extraction records no library items, and the review endorses this. Several objects the items define are in the pinned libraries:
- the rings B⁺_dR and B_dR, in Mathlib (items 3.1-bdr-reps and 3.1-bpdr);
- the Bruhat order on a Coxeter group, the longest element w₀ and the dot action w·λ = w(λ+ρ) − ρ, in Tau Ceti (item 2.1-setting);
- Verma modules M(μ) and their irreducible quotients L(μ), in Tau Ceti (item 2.4-category-O).

Five item notes point to the wrong source issue:
- 2.2.5-lci says 'see source issue E6', but the Proposition-cited-as-Lemma slip is E5;
- 2.4.7-bases says E7, but the Kazhdan–Lusztig index slip is E6;
- 2.5.2-component-detect says E7, but the η̂_{T_w} ambient-scheme slip is part of E5;
- 3.2-lattices-filtrations says E8, but the D_dR slip in (3.6) is E7;
- 3.2.5-regular-lattice says E8, but the missing α⁻¹ and 'Corollary 3.2.5' slips are E7.
The report says 'The remaining seven (E5–E11) are misprints' and then lists twelve slips. The review attributes the extraction to session cc-442dc5 ('Extraction under review: … by session cc-442dc5'; review.json: 'of the extraction by cc-442dc5'), while the extraction's own provenance line and the errata register name cc-fb70e5. The review also calls the Part II co-proposers 'three' in review.json 'changes' and 'two' in its notes; the Part II is co-proposed by two papers (PAPER-DING-25 route 4, PAPER-NEWTON-THORNE-21 route 4).

The route 7 items are planned at PG.3 and PG.7 only in part. PG.0–PG.3 are written for étale (φ,Γ)-modules and the Herr complex of a representation. PG.7 is written for the relative KPX category and its relative Herr complexes, and its accepted packet has no PG.7 node. Nothing in PG plans the following:
- (φ,Γ_K)-modules over R_{A,K}[1/t], i.e. modules with a stable R-lattice after inverting t (Definition 3.3.2);
- the category ΦΓ_{A,K} and the 'character type' objects R_{A,K}(δ)[1/t];
- the classification of the (φ,Γ_K)-submodules of R_{L,K}(δ)[1/t] as t^kR_{L,K}(δ);
- the colimit formula (3.11) and the Ext comparisons (3.12)–(3.13) after inverting t.
These are what §§3.3–3.5 run on.
